    "recommendations": "• Thin scattered trees around the house to create more open space between the trees and the structure.\n• Break up the two tree clusters nearest to the structure by removing select trees to reduce the concentration of vegetation in those areas.\n• Trim shrubs that are growing close to the house so they are no longer touching or immediately adjacent to the walls.\n• Remove or cut back the vegetation identified directly next to the structure on both sides.\n• Clear low-hanging branches from trees near the house so fire cannot climb from ground-level plants up into the tree canopy.\n• Keep the area along the curved driveway clear of overhanging branches and encroaching shrubs to maintain access for vehicles.\n• Thin scattered shrubs across the property to reduce connected patches of plants that could carry fire toward the structure.\n• Maintain wider open gaps between the scattered trees and the structure by removing the closest trees or heavy lower limbs.\n• Keep the open terrain areas around the structure free of dead plant material, fallen branches, and dry grass.\n• Clear vegetation along the edges of the curved driveway so emergency vehicles can navigate it without obstruction."
